content.text:
Walking the trace, log and metric data, I found one fault. The `attractions` pod went away during the incident and never came back, and the frontend's calls to it fail.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "attractions",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'attractions' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "The attractions service emits no spans at all in the abnormal window, versus 69 spans in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_deployment_name dep, metric, count(*) n, avg(value) v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_deployment_name = 'attractions' AND metric = 'k8s.deployment.available' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "The attractions deployment reports available=0 for all 16 abnormal samples, versus 1 in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'attractions.Attractions/%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend's calls to attractions (NearbyCinema, NearbyRest, NearbyMus) all end in Error, 488 spans in total."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level = 'ERROR' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend logs 304 ERROR lines in the abnormal window; no other service logs errors."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "attractions",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'HTTP /%' AND attr_status_code = 'Error' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "User-facing HTTP /cinema, /restaurants and /museums requests fail with Error at frontend, matching the attractions calls."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
